==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fa|en}} {{term|ستان|ـستان|tr=-estān|lang=fa}}, from {{etyl|pal|en}} {{term|-stʾn'|tr=-estān|lang=pal}}, from {{etyl|peo|en}} {{term|𐎿𐎫𐎠𐎴|tr=stāna-|lang=peo}}, from {{etyl|ira-pro|en}} {{m|ira-pro|*stāna-}}, from {{etyl|iir-pro|en}} {{m|iir-pro|*sthāna}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*steh₂-||to stand}}. Compare {{etyl|ae|-}} {{term|𐬯𐬙𐬁𐬥𐬀|tr=stāna-|lang=ae}}, {{etyl|sa|-}} {{term|स्थान|tr=sthā́na|lang=sa}}, English {{term|stay|lang=en}}, {{term|stand|lang=en}}, {{term|state|lang=en}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|en|suffix}}

# [[home]] of; [[place]] where one [[stay]]s; used especially in place names

====Usage notes====
Corresponding [[demonym]] usually formed by suffixing {{m|en|-i}}, yielding {{m|en||-stani}}. When the root is an ethnicity, the {{m|en||-stani}} form refers to the nationality, not ethnicity. Compare {{m|en|Tajik||member of Tajik ethnic group}} and {{m|en|Tajikistani||inhabitant of nation of Tajikistan}}.

